                    "url": "https://fluentcrm.com/"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "content": "If you want a **CRM with email automation**, the main thing to look for is a system that can **store contact and deal data** and **trigger personalized email sequences** based on behavior, timing, or pipeline stage.[5][12][15]\n\nCommon good-fit options include **HubSpot** for an all-in-one platform, **ActiveCampaign** for deeper automation, **Brevo** for low-cost high-volume sending, and **Klaviyo** if you are focused on B2C/ecommerce lifecycle messaging.[5][7][9]\n\nWhat \u201cCRM with email automation\u201d usually means:\n- A CRM keeps your contacts, deals, and history in one place.[5][7]\n- Email automation sends messages automatically when someone takes an action or reaches a stage, such as form submission, demo booking, or deal progression.[1][5][12]\n- The best setups log opens, replies, and clicks back into the CRM so future messages can be more targeted.[4][12][17]\n\nWhat to check before choosing one:\n- **Native email integration** with Gmail or Outlook for two-way sync.[4][6][8]\n- **Flexible triggers** such as time-based, behavior-based, and pipeline-stage automations.[6][10][12]\n- **Personalization** using CRM fields like name, company, deal stage, or last touchpoint.[2][8][17]\n- **Reporting** that connects email activity to sales outcomes and revenue.[7][10]\n- **Ease of setup** so you can build workflows without heavy IT help.[7][10]\n\nIf you want, I can narrow this down to:\n- **best free CRM with email automation**\n- **best for small business**\n- **best for sales follow-up**\n- **best for ecommerce**\n- **best for Gmail/Outlook integration**",
